{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>ויחשבה</b> Three times in the Masorah. See what I wrote in the perasha of Lekh Lekha." "<b> לזונה</b> Twice in the Masorah: ויחשבה לזונה · איכה היתה לזונה. Just as Tamar — beginning in disgrace and ultimately in honor, so too Jerusalem — her end is in honor, as written: ולכבוד אהיה בתוכה. And this is זאת קומתך, which resembles Tamar."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "Cross-reference to Ba'al HaTurim on Genesis 12:15 (perasha Lekh Lekha), where ויחשבה also appears.", 1 "The phrase זאת קומתך (Song of Songs 7:8) is read as an allusion to Tamar by letter-association; the terse juxtaposition is preserved as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:00.294639814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}